    given-names: Paul
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher, London, United Kingdom"
keywords:
  - systemic cyber risk
  - global sensitivity analysis
  - Sobol indices
  - Morris screening
  - response surface validation
  - Cyber Triangle
  - simulation
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Brittle, not broken: source code (PhDPaper4C)"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23669511"
  - type: data
    title: "Brittle, not broken: specifications, protocols and run outputs"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23669054"
abstract: >
  Analysis code over a frozen simulated estate model (model digest d3f90805edfee3c7, deposited at
  doi:10.5281/zenodo.23669511): a global sensitivity programme (Morris screen with exposure strata,
  two-pass Sobol decomposition with a pre-set incidental rule, chunked pair-and-square response surface,
  data-derived groups); the surface's validation (hold-out by base-row family, additive-against-pairwise
  comparison, ridge-penalty scan, a fresh-draw surface mode in which every configuration receives its own
  estate and random stream, a noise-ceiling estimator and a paired worked example); a declared exploratory
  timing revision (attack-transition opportunity interval and one-off mobilisation lag) over the unchanged
  engine; and a mechanism-validation package (exact checkpoints and branches, disturbance and capacity
  interventions, forced plane capture, three audits). The model itself is not changed by anything here.
